include Readme.md
include requirements.txt
include LICENSE
# Bundle the v1 ingest schema with the sdist. The wheel picks it up via
# setup.py's package_data once schema/__init__.py exists, but sdists go
# through MANIFEST.in — without this line a source distribution would
# be missing the schema and any consumer building from sdist (some
# air-gapped pip installs do this) would hit the same FileNotFoundError
# the wheel bug surfaced in cluster testing.
recursive-include tracebloc_ingestor/schema *.json
# Keep the unit-test suite out of the sdist. setup.py's find_packages(include=)
# keeps `tests` out of the WHEEL, but the sdist goes through a different code
# path: distutils' sdist.add_defaults() picks up tests/test*.py on its own,
# whatever `packages=` says. Measured: with include= alone the wheel was clean
# and the sdist still carried 100 tests/ members. scripts/check_dist_contents.py
# reads both artefacts in the publish workflows, which is how this was caught.
prune tests
